          <attvalue for="36" value="Higher rates of ship rerouting impose additional transit costs and delivery delays that force energy‑exporting governments to provide emergency liquidity support, subsidies or bridge financing for exporters and importers, raising near‑term borrowing needs and rollover pressure." />
